  "description": "Reid MTB Elite | 27.5\" mountain bike\nBuilt for trail riding, off-road adventures and everyday cycling – the Reid Bikes MTB Elite combines a lightweight alloy frame, reliable components and confident handling.\nThe Reid Bikes MTB Elite is designed for riders looking for a versatile mountain bike for exploring trails, tackling uneven terrain and enjoying everyday rides. Featuring a lightweight Alloy 6061 frame with internal cable routing and 27.5\" wheels, it offers a comfortable and controlled riding experience across a range of surfaces.\nA Uding suspension fork with 100mm of travel helps absorb bumps and uneven terrain, providing added comfort and control when riding off-road. The wide 700mm alloy riser handlebars offer a stable steering position, while 2.35\" all-terrain MTB tyres provide reliable grip across trails, gravel paths and other mixed surfaces.\nAn 8-speed Shimano drivetrain with an upgraded 32T single chainset and 11–40T cassette provides a practical range of gears for tackling climbs and enjoying flatter sections of trail. Tektro HD-M275 hydraulic disc brakes with 160mm rotors deliver reliable, controlled stopping power, while double-wall alloy rims provide added durability for regular riding.\nWhether you're exploring local trails, riding off-road routes or enjoying weekend adventures, the Reid Bikes MTB Elite offers a versatile combination of comfort, control and dependable mountain bike performance.\nThe Reid Bikes MTB Elite is ideal for:\n\nTrail riding and off-road adventures, with 100mm suspension travel to help absorb bumps and uneven terrain\n\nRiders looking for a versatile mountain bike, with a lightweight Alloy 6061 frame and 27.5\" wheels\n\nTackling climbs and descents, with an 8-speed Shimano drivetrain and 32T single chainset\n\nRiding across mixed surfaces, with 2.35\" all-terrain MTB tyres for reliable grip and stability\n\nControlled braking, with Tektro hydraulic disc brakes and 160mm rotors\n\nComfortable, confident handling, with wide 700mm alloy riser handlebars and front suspension\n\nWeekend rides and everyday adventures, with a versatile setup suited to trails, paths and recreational cycling",
